<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian Stocks to Watch Today - Sept 5.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian Stocks to Watch Today - Sept 5.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Some Australian stocks to watch this morning:</p>
<p>*Boral A$3.01 (steady)</p>
<p>Prior to trading opening, the building materials group reported a 43.9 percent lower full year pre-tax profit of A$248.63 million.</p>
<p>*Goodman Fielder A$1.30 (-.01)</p>
<p>Bakery/food group reported a full year net profit of A$28.3 million, including an abnormal loss of A$72.2 million before trading opened.</p>
<p>*AWA A$0.75 (+.01)</p>
<p>Gambling and electronics group due to report full year profit figures later today.</p>
<p>*Publishing and Broadcasting A$6.05 (+.15)</p>
<p>Packer-controlled media reported a 50 percent higher full year net profit of A$225.39 million on Wednesday, slightly better than market expectations.</p>
<p>*Woodside A$7.74 (+.06)</p>
<p>Oil and gas major on Wednesday turned in a sharply higher firts half net profit of A$84.38 million.</p>
<p>*TNT A$1.47 (+.03)</p>
<p>On Wednesday, troubled transport/logistics group reported a sharply lower full year net profit of A$9.84 million but said the sale of its stake in the Ansett airline would produce strong growth in the current year.</p>
<p>*QCT Resources A$1.74 (+.04)</p>
<p>Major coal miner reported a sharply higher full year net profit of A$71.47 million, citing higher selling prices and higher volumes for the jump.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
